{"parentUuid":"a801780a-7216-4a35-9a7a-90d67352e251","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2aba288e-182f-4542-ac86-e9a5b1e2f8df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S2LWDa7UCbCXvfHfTn2atb","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Hidaayat Williams\\.claude\\plans\\i-m-doing-a-take-home-drifting-muffin.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"1a0280ea-9046-4710-843e-f5483bc4d7e7","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:59:04.540Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Hidaayat Williams\\.claude\\plans\\i-m-doing-a-take-home-drifting-muffin.md","oldString":"**CLAUDE.md is the authoritative spec** and is used as the single source of truth below.\nThe PDF could not be read programmatically (it embeds subset fonts; body text is not\nrecoverable as plain text without a PDF library, and the file is marked confidential so it\nmust not be quoted or committed anyway). I verified the key data facts directly instead.","newString":"**CLAUDE.md is the authoritative spec** and is used as the single source of truth below.\nThe PDF could not be read programmatically (it embeds subset fonts; body text is not\nrecoverable as plain text without a PDF library, and the file is marked confidential so it\nmust not be quoted or committed anyway). The user confirmed the problem statement in prose and\nit matches CLAUDE.md; proceeding from CLAUDE.md. I verified the key data facts directly.\n\nExtra points the user made explicit (consistent with CLAUDE.md, restated here so they aren't lost):\n- **Both** the input CSV (`data/results.csv`) and the output CSV (`out/week10_table.csv`) must be committed.\n- Automated tests are mandatory.\n- Use only common package managers; never commit installed packages; document any non-trivial setup in the README.\n- Deliverables include an `ai/` folder of conversation history and `AI_REFLECTION.md` (human-written).\n- The solution must be explainable in a review → keep functions small, pure, and obvious; no clever one-liners.","originalFile":"# Football League Table — build plan\n\n## Context\n\nTake-home assessment. Goal: a production-quality, stdlib-only Python 3.10+ CLI that reads\nfootball match results (CSV) and writes a league standings table (CSV), used to produce the\n**1974/75 English First Division table for week 10** (and any other week).\n\nCurrent repo is greenfield: only `CLAUDE.md`, `data/raw/results_raw.txt`, `.gitignore`,\n`.gitattributes`, and the gitignored, confidential `docs/problem_statement.pdf` exist.\nEverything else (the `league/` package, `tools/convert_raw.py`, tests, fixtures, `data/results.csv`,\n`out/week10_table.csv`, README, CI) must be built.\n\n**CLAUDE.md is the authoritative spec** and is used as the single source of truth below.\nThe PDF could not be read programmatically (it embeds subset fonts; body text is not\nrecoverable as plain text without a PDF library, and the file is marked confidential so it\nmust not be quoted or committed anyway). I verified the key data facts directly instead.\n\n### Verified data facts (from `data/raw/results_raw.txt`)\n- 19 date headers, 148 match lines, 22 distinct teams, dates strictly ascending. ✅ matches CLAUDE.md.\n- Match-line heuristic (\"tab-split fields 2 and 3 are integers\") cleanly excludes `Lineups`/scorer lines.\n\n## Domain rules (do NOT modernise)\n- Win = 2 pts (configurable via `--points-per-win`), draw = 1, loss = 0.\n- Rank by: points desc, then **goal average** = goals_for / goals_against (higher better), then team name A–Z.\n- Goal average: GA 0 & GF>0 → `inf` (ranks first among equals, printed `inf`); 0/0 → `0.0`; else 3 decimals.\n- `--tiebreak goal-average|goal-difference`, default `goal-average`.\n- Week N = `(date - season_start).days // 7 + 1`; table for week N includes all matches with `week <= N`.\n- `--season-start` defaults to earliest match date (1974-08-17); README/committed command passes it explicitly.\n- `--until YYYY-MM-DD` = include matches on/before that date; mutually exclusive with `--week`; exactly one required.\n\n## Architecture (target)\n```\nleague/__init__.py\nleague/__main__.py      # thin: delegates to cli.main()\nleague/models.py        # Match, TeamRecord, Rules dataclasses (type-hinted)\nleague/parsing.py       # CSV rows -> list[Match] with validation (row-numbered errors)\nleague/table.py         # pure standings logic, no I/O (build + rank)\nleague/output.py        # format/write table as CSV (3dp, inf, \\n endings)\nleague/cli.py           # argparse, stdin/stdout, week/until logic, error reporting\ntools/convert_raw.py    # raw text -> data/results.csv, reports match counts per date\ntests/                  # pytest + fixtures/\nREADME.md               # setup, run, assumptions, sourcing/verification, CI badge\n.github/workflows/ci.yml\n```\n\n## Cross-platform invariants (dev on Windows, verified on macOS via CI)\n- Always `open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\")`; CSV writer `lineterminator=\"\\n\"`.\n- Reconfigure stdin/stdout to UTF-8 and stdout to `\\n`; accept LF/CRLF and a UTF-8 BOM on input.\n- Stdlib only at runtime (`csv`, `argparse`, `dataclasses`, `datetime`, `sys`, `pathlib`).\n- No 3.11+ features; Python floor 3.10. No shell scripts / `.bat` / `.ps1` / `os.system`.\n- Local runs use `.venv\\Scripts\\python ...`; README/CI use `python3` / `.venv/bin/python`.\n\n## Step-by-step plan (small commits)\n\n1. **Scaffold + tooling.** `.venv`, `requirements-dev.txt` (pytest, ruff), `pyproject`/`ruff` config,\n   empty `league/` package, `out/.gitkeep`. Confirm `.gitignore`/`.gitattributes` cover `.venv/`,\n   caches, `out/*.tmp`, the PDF. _Commit: \"Add project scaffold and dev tooling\"._\n2. **Models.** `league/models.py`: `Match`, `TeamRecord`, `Rules` dataclasses + a `goal_average`\n   helper (handles inf / 0.0). Unit tests for the helper. _Commit: \"Add domain models\"._\n3. **Parsing + validation.** `league/parsing.py`: read CSV rows → `Match`, with row-numbered errors\n   for every rule in CLAUDE.md (bad columns, empty names, non-int/negative scores, bad dates,\n   self-play, duplicate same-date fixture, backwards dates). BOM/CRLF tolerant. Tests first. _Commit: \"Add CSV parsing and validation\"._\n4. **Table logic.** `league/table.py`: pure functions to accumulate records and rank by the rules\n   (points → goal average/difference → name). Week/`--until` filtering as a pure predicate.\n   Tests for points, ranking, tie-breaks, GA edge cases, week cutoff, empty input. _Commit: \"Add standings computation\"._\n5. **Output.** `league/output.py`: format rows (`position,team,played,won,drawn,lost,goals_for,\n   goals_against,goal_average,points`), 3dp / `inf`, UTF-8 `\\n`. Tests compare exact text. _Commit: \"Add CSV output\"._\n6. **CLI.** `league/cli.py` + `__main__.py`: argparse, stdin/stdout defaults, mutually-exclusive\n   `--week`/`--until`, `--season-start`/`--points-per-win`/`--tiebreak`, exit codes, `error: ...`\n   to stderr (no stack traces). CLI usage-error tests. _Commit: \"Add CLI\"._\n7. **Raw converter.** `tools/convert_raw.py`: raw → `data/results.csv`, skipping `Lineups`/scorer\n   lines (fields 2&3 integer rule), trimming trailing spaces, printing per-date match counts.\n   Tests on messy sample lines. Generate and commit `data/results.csv`. _Commit: \"Add raw converter and cleaned results\"._\n8. **Fixtures + end-to-end.** Produce `out/week10_table.csv`, `tests/fixtures/week10_expected.csv`,\n   `week5_expected.csv`; assert the CLAUDE.md sanity checks hold (Liverpool P13 9-1-3 21-8 2.625 19pts;\n   Leicester fewest at P12; Ipswich week-5 lead 12pts 3.250). E2E tests via file and stdin/stdout,\n   plus the `--season-start` and `--until` equivalence cases. _Commit: \"Add week 5/10 fixtures and end-to-end tests\"._\n9. **Docs + CI.** `README.md` (setup, run commands, assumptions, data sourcing/verification, CI badge,\n   Windows-dev/macOS-CI note, how to get 3.10+ on macOS) and `.github/workflows/ci.yml`\n   (ubuntu+macos × 3.10/3.12: venv, install, pytest, run CLI for week 10, `diff` vs committed output).\n   _Commit: \"Add README and CI\"._\n10. **Fresh-clone check.** Clone to a temp dir, follow README verbatim, confirm tests pass, lint clean,\n    week-10 output reproduces. Fix anything. _Commit only if changes needed._\n\n## Guardrails (from CLAUDE.md)\n- Never invent/guess/\"fix\" a result, team or date from memory; flag anomalies for the human.\n- Never edit `tests/fixtures/*` or `data/results.csv` to make a test pass.\n- Do not generate `AI_REFLECTION.md` (human writes it); do not commit/quote the PDF.\n- Keep `.claude/` and `ai/` (submission artefacts); no employer/company names anywhere.\n\n## Verification\n- `ruff check . && ruff format --check .` clean.\n- `python3 -m pytest` green from a fresh clone using only README steps.\n- Week-10 CLI output byte-identical to committed `out/week10_table.csv`; fixtures match sanity checks.\n- CI green on ubuntu-latest + macos-latest, Python 3.10 and 3.12.\n\n## Open risk to resolve\nExpected fixtures don't exist yet and the real source standings aren't accessible here, so the\nonly independent oracle is the set of numeric sanity checks in CLAUDE.md. Plan is to build the\ntable, assert those sanity checks, and treat the generated tables as fixtures only once they pass —\nflagging any mismatch rather than editing data to fit.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":8,"newStart":14,"newLines":16,"lines":[" **CLAUDE.md is the authoritative spec** and is used as the single source of truth below."," The PDF could not be read programmatically (it embeds subset fonts; body text is not"," recoverable as plain text without a PDF library, and the file is marked confidential so it","-must not be quoted or committed anyway). I verified the key data facts directly instead.","+must not be quoted or committed anyway). The user confirmed the problem statement in prose and","+it matches CLAUDE.md; proceeding from CLAUDE.md. I verified the key data facts directly."," ","+Extra points the user made explicit (consistent with CLAUDE.md, restated here so they aren't lost):","+- **Both** the input CSV (`data/results.csv`) and the output CSV (`out/week10_table.csv`) must be committed.","+- Automated tests are mandatory.","+- Use only common package managers; never commit installed packages; document any non-trivial setup in the README.","+- Deliverables include an `ai/` folder of conversation history and `AI_REFLECTION.md` (human-written).","+- The solution must be explainable in a review → keep functions small, pure, and obvious; no clever one-liners.","+"," ### Verified data facts (from `data/raw/results_raw.txt`)"," - 19 date headers, 148 match lines, 22 distinct teams, dates strictly ascending. ✅ matches CLAUDE.md."," - Match-line heuristic (\"tab-split fields 2 and 3 are integers\") cleanly excludes `Lineups`/scorer lines."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a801780a-7216-4a35-9a7a-90d67352e251","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Hidaayat Williams\\IdeaProjects\\football-league-table","sessionId":"13005604-e4fd-4768-8817-b92b29c9b503","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"i-m-doing-a-take-home-drifting-muffin"}
