{"parentUuid":"c1824542-39ec-4903-bedd-ebc95f6ea290","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cfu7keNmGcihH5DU9DpR7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FsCAwQERgTD6M11RqDNm22","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Hidaayat Williams\\IdeaProjects\\football-league-table\\README.md","content":"# Football League Table\n\n[![CI](https://github.com/Horizyn77/football-league-table/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/Horizyn77/football-league-table/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n\nA small command-line tool that reads football match results (CSV) and writes a league\nstandings table (CSV). It is used to produce the **English First Division table for week 10\nof the 1974/75 season**, but it works for any week of any season you feed it.\n\nThe runtime uses the **Python standard library only**. `pytest` and `ruff` are needed for\ndevelopment, not to run the program.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Python **3.10 or newer**.\n\nmacOS ships an older `python3`, so install a current one first if needed:\n\n```bash\nbrew install python@3.12\n# or, with pyenv:\npyenv install 3.12.6 && pyenv local 3.12.6\n```\n\nCheck your version:\n\n```bash\npython3 --version\n```\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements-dev.txt\n```\n\n(The program itself needs no dependencies; this installs the test and lint tools.)\n\n## Produce the week 10 table\n\nWith files:\n\n```bash\npython3 -m league --input data/results.csv --week 10 --season-start 1974-08-17 --output out/week10_table.csv\n```\n\nThe same result using stdin/stdout and the date-based cutoff (week 10 ended 1974-10-19):\n\n```bash\npython3 -m league --until 1974-10-19 --season-start 1974-08-17 < data/results.csv > out/week10_table.csv\n```\n\n`out/week10_table.csv` is committed; CI regenerates it and fails if it changes.\n\n## Usage\n\n```\npython3 -m league [--input FILE] [--output FILE] (--week N | --until YYYY-MM-DD)\n    [--season-start YYYY-MM-DD] [--points-per-win N]\n    [--tiebreak goal-average|goal-difference]\n```\n\n- `--input` / `--output` default to stdin / stdout.\n- Exactly one of `--week N` or `--until YYYY-MM-DD` is required.\n  - `--week N` includes every match in weeks 1..N.\n  - `--until DATE` includes every match played on or before `DATE`.\n- `--season-start` sets the date week 1 begins; it defaults to the earliest match date in\n  the input. The commands above pass it explicitly so the week numbering never depends on how\n  much of the season the input file contains.\n- `--points-per-win` defaults to `2` (the 1974/75 rule).\n- `--tiebreak` defaults to `goal-average` (the 1974/75 rule); `goal-difference` is also available.\n\nOn bad input or usage the program prints `error: <reason>` to stderr and exits non-zero,\nwithout a stack trace.\n\n## Output format\n\nCSV with the header:\n\n```\nposition,team,played,won,drawn,lost,goals_for,goals_against,goal_average,points\n```\n\nRows are in rank order. `goal_average` has three decimals, or the literal `inf` when a team\nhas conceded no goals but scored at least one. Output is UTF-8 with `\\n` line endings.\n\n## Ranking rules (1974/75, not modern)\n\n1. **Points**: 2 for a win, 1 for a draw, 0 for a loss. (Three points per win began in 1981.)\n2. **Goal average** = goals for ÷ goals against, higher is better. Goal *difference* was not\n   used until 1976/77.\n3. **Team name**, alphabetically (A–Z), so exact ties are deterministic — e.g. Burnley is\n   placed above Newcastle United at week 10.\n\nGoal-average edge cases: no goals conceded with goals scored is infinite (`inf`, ranks first\namong equals); no goals either way is `0.0`.\n\n## Regenerating the cleaned input\n\n`data/results.csv` is produced from the raw pasted text with:\n\n```bash\npython3 tools/convert_raw.py\n```\n\nIt keeps only lines whose 2nd and 3rd tab-separated fields are whole numbers (so scorer and\n`Lineups` lines are skipped) and prints a per-date match-count report.\n\n## Tests and lint\n\n```bash\npython3 -m pytest\nruff check . && ruff format --check .\n```\n\n## Data: sourcing and verification\n\n- `data/raw/results_raw.txt` — the raw results as pasted, one `== YYYY-MM-DD ==` block per\n  matchday.\n- `data/results.csv` — the cleaned input (148 matches, 22 teams), generated by\n  `tools/convert_raw.py`.\n- `tests/fixtures/week5_expected.csv` and `week10_expected.csv` — the official First Division\n  standings for 1974-09-14 and 1974-10-19 from\n  [englishfootballleaguetables.co.uk](https://www.englishfootballleaguetables.co.uk/).\n\nThe end-to-end tests assert the program reproduces both official tables exactly, and cross-check\nindependent sanity facts (after week 10 Liverpool are played 13, 9-1-3, 21–8, goal average 2.625,\n19 points, and Leicester City have the fewest games played at 12; after week 5 Ipswich Town lead\non 12 points and a 3.250 goal average).\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- A match line in the raw data is one whose 2nd and 3rd tab fields are integers; everything else\n  (scorers, `Lineups`, notes) is ignored.\n- Teams can have played a different number of games within the same week because of midweek\n  fixtures. This is expected, not an error.\n- The input contains only First Division league matches (no cup or international games).\n- Input rows are in non-decreasing date order; the program rejects dates that go backwards.\n- The input CSV includes the header row shown above.\n\n## Development notes\n\n- Developed on Windows; macOS and Linux are verified by CI (Ubuntu and macOS, Python 3.10 and\n  3.12). CI runs the tests and regenerates the week 10 table to confirm it matches the committed\n  output.\n- `AI_REFLECTION.md` is written by the author. The `ai/` folder holds the AI-assisted\n  development conversation history.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2426,"cache_read_input_tokens":197223,"output_tokens":2165,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2426,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2165,"cache_read_input_tokens":197223,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2426},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FsCAwQERgTD6M11RqDNm22":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Hidaayat Williams\\IdeaProjects\\football-league-table\\README.md","content":"# Football League Table\n\n[![CI](https://github.com/Horizyn77/football-league-table/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/Horizyn77/football-league-table/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n\nA small command-line tool that reads football match results (CSV) and writes a league\nstandings table (CSV). It is used to produce the **English First Division table for week 10\nof the 1974/75 season**, but it works for any week of any season you feed it.\n\nThe runtime uses the **Python standard library only**. `pytest` and `ruff` are needed for\ndevelopment, not to run the program.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Python **3.10 or newer**.\n\nmacOS ships an older `python3`, so install a current one first if needed:\n\n```bash\nbrew install python@3.12\n# or, with pyenv:\npyenv install 3.12.6 && pyenv local 3.12.6\n```\n\nCheck your version:\n\n```bash\npython3 --version\n```\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements-dev.txt\n```\n\n(The program itself needs no dependencies; this installs the test and lint tools.)\n\n## Produce the week 10 table\n\nWith files:\n\n```bash\npython3 -m league --input data/results.csv --week 10 --season-start 1974-08-17 --output out/week10_table.csv\n```\n\nThe same result using stdin/stdout and the date-based cutoff (week 10 ended 1974-10-19):\n\n```bash\npython3 -m league --until 1974-10-19 --season-start 1974-08-17 < data/results.csv > out/week10_table.csv\n```\n\n`out/week10_table.csv` is committed; CI regenerates it and fails if it changes.\n\n## Usage\n\n```\npython3 -m league [--input FILE] [--output FILE] (--week N | --until YYYY-MM-DD)\n    [--season-start YYYY-MM-DD] [--points-per-win N]\n    [--tiebreak goal-average|goal-difference]\n```\n\n- `--input` / `--output` default to stdin / stdout.\n- Exactly one of `--week N` or `--until YYYY-MM-DD` is required.\n  - `--week N` includes every match in weeks 1..N.\n  - `--until DATE` includes every match played on or before `DATE`.\n- `--season-start` sets the date week 1 begins; it defaults to the earliest match date in\n  the input. The commands above pass it explicitly so the week numbering never depends on how\n  much of the season the input file contains.\n- `--points-per-win` defaults to `2` (the 1974/75 rule).\n- `--tiebreak` defaults to `goal-average` (the 1974/75 rule); `goal-difference` is also available.\n\nOn bad input or usage the program prints `error: <reason>` to stderr and exits non-zero,\nwithout a stack trace.\n\n## Output format\n\nCSV with the header:\n\n```\nposition,team,played,won,drawn,lost,goals_for,goals_against,goal_average,points\n```\n\nRows are in rank order. `goal_average` has three decimals, or the literal `inf` when a team\nhas conceded no goals but scored at least one. Output is UTF-8 with `\\n` line endings.\n\n## Ranking rules (1974/75, not modern)\n\n1. **Points**: 2 for a win, 1 for a draw, 0 for a loss. (Three points per win began in 1981.)\n2. **Goal average** = goals for ÷ goals against, higher is better. Goal *difference* was not\n   used until 1976/77.\n3. **Team name**, alphabetically (A–Z), so exact ties are deterministic — e.g. Burnley is\n   placed above Newcastle United at week 10.\n\nGoal-average edge cases: no goals conceded with goals scored is infinite (`inf`, ranks first\namong equals); no goals either way is `0.0`.\n\n## Regenerating the cleaned input\n\n`data/results.csv` is produced from the raw pasted text with:\n\n```bash\npython3 tools/convert_raw.py\n```\n\nIt keeps only lines whose 2nd and 3rd tab-separated fields are whole numbers (so scorer and\n`Lineups` lines are skipped) and prints a per-date match-count report.\n\n## Tests and lint\n\n```bash\npython3 -m pytest\nruff check . && ruff format --check .\n```\n\n## Data: sourcing and verification\n\n- `data/raw/results_raw.txt` — the raw results as pasted, one `== YYYY-MM-DD ==` block per\n  matchday.\n- `data/results.csv` — the cleaned input (148 matches, 22 teams), generated by\n  `tools/convert_raw.py`.\n- `tests/fixtures/week5_expected.csv` and `week10_expected.csv` — the official First Division\n  standings for 1974-09-14 and 1974-10-19 from\n  [englishfootballleaguetables.co.uk](https://www.englishfootballleaguetables.co.uk/).\n\nThe end-to-end tests assert the program reproduces both official tables exactly, and cross-check\nindependent sanity facts (after week 10 Liverpool are played 13, 9-1-3, 21–8, goal average 2.625,\n19 points, and Leicester City have the fewest games played at 12; after week 5 Ipswich Town lead\non 12 points and a 3.250 goal average).\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- A match line in the raw data is one whose 2nd and 3rd tab fields are integers; everything else\n  (scorers, `Lineups`, notes) is ignored.\n- Teams can have played a different number of games within the same week because of midweek\n  fixtures. This is expected, not an error.\n- The input contains only First Division league matches (no cup or international games).\n- Input rows are in non-decreasing date order; the program rejects dates that go backwards.\n- The input CSV includes the header row shown above.\n\n## Development notes\n\n- Developed on Windows; macOS and Linux are verified by CI (Ubuntu and macOS, Python 3.10 and\n  3.12). CI runs the tests and regenerates the week 10 table to confirm it matches the committed\n  output.\n- `AI_REFLECTION.md` is written by the author. The `ai/` folder holds the AI-assisted\n  development conversation history.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfu7kdzCo6Vb7k4xGUs6s","requestedModel":"claude-opus-4-8","type":"assistant","uuid":"30e07ed5-8fad-4646-a939-060e366f66b8","timestamp":"2026-10-10T19:35:17.916Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Hidaayat Williams\\IdeaProjects\\football-league-table","sessionId":"13005604-e4fd-4768-8817-b92b29c9b503","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"i-m-doing-a-take-home-drifting-muffin"}
